vqa_ring is independently written; no rustix or x11rb source is copied.
Non-trivial syscall/lifetime patterns were adapted from the design's citations:

rustix 1.1.5 (a1c13cc1), Apache-2.0 OR MIT:
  src/fs/memfd_create.rs:20 — CLOEXEC + ALLOW_SEALING creation
  src/fs/fcntl.rs:57,73 — receive-side seal verification / adding seals
  src/mm/mmap.rs:87 — shared mapping ownership
  src/net/send_recv/msg.rs:299,496,789 — SCM_RIGHTS and rejected fd ownership
  src/net/sockopt.rs:1692 — SO_PEERCRED
  src/thread/futex.rs:45-62,86,569-575 — relative wait / shared wake / waitv
  src/backend/linux_raw/thread/syscalls.rs:349-362 — absolute waitv deadline
  src/time/clock.rs:60 — CLOCK_MONOTONIC

x11rb 0.14.0 (86c4252f), Apache-2.0 OR MIT:
  src/rust_connection/stream.rs:304-311 — EINTR retry pattern

Coordinates and licence identifiers are cited from the supplied design and
stage-2 packs; source trees were not fetched or vendored. libc replaces rustix's
safe wrappers, typed flags, ancillary buffer and timespec abstractions. All
unsafe code (including syscall test helpers) is confined to src/map.rs.
